arison of two objects based on shared attributes leading to an inference about other attributes.\n\nD) \"Silver and copper are both metals with electrical conductivity, but the resistivity of silver is lower, so silver is more suitable to be a conductive material than copper.\"\n- This option does not fit the definition of an analogical argument. It is a comparison based on a specific property (electrical conductivity) and concludes that silver is more suitable for a conductive material than copper. There is no comparison of two objects based on shared attributes leading to an inference about other attributes.\n\nAfter analyzing all the options, the correct answer is:\n</think>\n<answer>\nB\n</answer>",
