n.\n\nC) **When users who forget their passwords are locked out of their own accounts, they must often go through a complicated process in order to have their accounts unlocked.**\n   - This option discusses the process of unlocking accounts but does not directly relate to the risk of unauthorized access due to written passwords. It does not support the overall conclusion about the necessity of complex passwords.\n\nD) **People who use mnemonic devices to help remember their passwords are able to easily remember passwords that are long, complex, and unpredictable.**\n   - This option discusses the use of mnemonic devices but does not address the risk of unauthorized access due to written passwords. It does not support the overall conclusion.\n\nAfter analyzing each option, the one that strongly supports the overall conclusion is option B.\n</think>\n<answer>\nB\n</answer>",
