de with a new conditional statement based on the negation of the original statement.\n\nD) If the lottery were fair, the person who won the lottery would not have been likely to win it. thus, since this person would have been likely to win the lottery if it were unfair, the lottery was probably unfair.\n- This option follows the contrapositive pattern. It presents a conditional statement and its negation, and then concludes with a new conditional statement based on the negation of the original statement.\n\nAfter analyzing all the options, the pattern of reasoning in the argument above is most similar to that in option D.\n</think>\n<answer>\nD\n</answer>",
