anies, not the average job creation rate.\n\nD) The number of jobs created in the derderian economy last year was substantially larger than the number of jobs lost.\n- This option talks about the net change in jobs last year (jobs created minus jobs lost). However, the argument is about the number of new companies starting up this year and whether it will break the record. This option does not directly support the argument's conclusion.\n\nThe assumption that the argument relies on is that the number of new companies starting up is crucial for breaking the record. The correct assumption is that the number of new companies starting up this year must be a record number to break the record for new jobs created. This is the only option that directly supports the argument's conclusion.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.\n</think>\n<answer>\nD\n</answer>",
